TITLE:: RCMidi
summary:: MIDI CC control of a song, with 14-bit fine pairing
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCSong, Classes/RCKeyboardState

DESCRIPTION::
The proto-library's code::control_synth:: / code::control_midi:: / code::control_attribute::. Every MIDIdef made here is remembered by name and freed by link::#-free:: / link::#-freeAll::. code::fine: true:: pairs cc with cc + 32 (LSB).

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: pairWait
Seconds an MSB waits for its LSB before it fires alone (0.02).
METHOD:: findSrcId
uid of a MIDI source by name; nil when absent, with a warning unless code::warn:: is false.
argument:: deviceName
argument:: warn
METHOD:: absentID
The source filter of a mapping whose device is absent: never a source's uid, so nothing reaches it until link::#-rebind::.
METHOD:: sourceList
The sources looked through (nil: code::MIDIClient.sources::); a test stands a list in for them.
METHOD:: connectFunc
How link::#-rebind:: connects a found source: code::{ |index, endpoint| }:: (nil: code::MIDIIn.connect::); a test stands in for it.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: control
argument:: name
argument:: ccNum
argument:: chan
argument:: deviceName
The source the mapping listens to; nil: every source. A device named and absent: the mapping is made whole (link::#-replay:: works) but listens to nothing, with a warning, until it is plugged in and link::#-rebind:: called (HL3-P8, Nov 19 2026: it listened to every source, and another device's CCs drove knobs into takes).
argument:: valFunc
Maps the raw value (0..127, fractional with fine).
argument:: action
Receives code::(value, raw)::.
argument:: fine
True: the value is msb + lsb/128, the MSB on code::ccNum::, its LSB on code::ccNum + 32::, in that order, as the MIDI spec sends them. An MSB sets the LSB to 0 and the LSB that follows completes the value: the LSB fires (alone too, a fine move on the last MSB); an MSB fires only when no LSB comes within link::#*pairWait:: (a sender may leave out an LSB of 0).
argument:: throttle
Seconds, nil by default (every message fires). A knob turn sends tens of messages per second, twice as many with code::fine::, and an action over a whole batch (code::batch.editAttr::) costs milliseconds each, which starves the clock: with a throttle the first message fires at once, the ones arriving within the window are swallowed and the last of them fires when the window closes, re-arming while messages keep coming. 0.02 to 0.05 s is inaudible on a knob.
METHOD:: controlSynth
argument:: synth
argument:: attr
nil sets the value itself (buses).
argument:: setNothing
argument:: throttle
As for link::#-control::.
METHOD:: controlAttribute
code::object[key] = value:: for dictionaries, code::object.key_(value):: otherwise.
argument:: throttle
As for link::#-control::.
METHOD:: free
argument:: name
METHOD:: rebind
After plugging a device in: the sources listed again, each found device's source connected (a session connects the sources there are at its start, not one plugged in later), the mappings that waited for it made again on its uid. Returns their names; the others keep waiting (link::#-pending::).
code::
~song.midi.rebind;
::
METHOD:: pending
Name → the arguments of a mapping waiting for its absent device.
METHOD:: freeAll
